        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Never Alone (video game)\n- People: Nuna\n- Animals: Arctic fox, Vulpes lagopus\n- Places: Arctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere, Arctic tundra biome\n- Concepts: puzzle gameplay, eight-chapter story\n\nFacts:\n- Never Alone is a video game in which the player swaps between an Iñupiaq girl named Nuna and her Arctic fox companion.\n- Never Alone has puzzle gameplay within a story that spans eight chapters.\n- The Arctic fox, also called Vulpes lagopus, white fox, polar fox, or snow fox, is a small fox.\n- The Arctic fox is native to the Arctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere and is common throughout the Arctic tundra biome.",
